  "findings": [
    {
      "check": "Exact source route and checked state",
      "result": "PASS_SOURCE_ONLY",
      "detail": "leaf_prefix returns split word=pre++[bit], the actual RoutedEntry and uniform run. The sketch destructures RoutedEntry in its actual five-witness/seven-conjunct order. Its split gives dropLast=pre\u2032; portState_of_path uses the complete internal RolePath and role lookup, then r.state=q\u2032. Equality of the two some-values identifies q\u2032 with the requested q. No short-suffix or physical-state-only inference replaces the route."
    },
    {
      "check": "Exact complete-word physical port",
      "result": "PASS_SOURCE_ONLY",
      "detail": "conc_leafPort yields zc q (pre.reverse++[true]) (bit::replicate (n+(D0-(pre.length+1))) false++true::sepsR vs). FrameContracts.leafPort on word=pre++[bit] has the same reversed tail, final head bit, leading marker, header and registers. D0=64 and length(word)=length(pre)+1 give precisely n+(64-word.length), including Nat subtraction saturation. There is no Valid premise or length restriction on this prefix theorem; current leaf_prefix already proves the same uniform run for arbitrary n/vs."
    },
    {
      "check": "Progress and future full caller contract",
      "result": "PASS_SOURCE_ONLY_PLAN",
      "detail": "The sketch concludes Reach using the existential run clock and does not assert it positive. Packet all_caller_standard supplies Reach1 from the exact same full-word port; current Reach.trans_reach1 preserves positive progress after composition. caller_bindings gives the walk ending at exactly word.length and the same portState check; current walk_root/twalk_leafAt/consume correspondence can recover LeafAt on that complete consumed word. CallerOK.2.1 supplies length <=48."
    },
    {
      "check": "Break domain guard and target gap",
      "result": "PASS_SOURCE_ONLY_PLAN",
      "detail": "Shape contains sourceGuard. Its break branch supplies both argument <= suffix.count false and a false bit in the stripped suffix. With CallerOK.word=prefix++suffix, stripPath_append transfers this witness into the full stripped word, forcing allOnes=false. This guard is necessary to match the residual no-overflow gap to tgtConf; continue has overflow=false by definition. conc_target with growth(.plain .none)=0 and boxList(.plain .none)=sepsR supplies the proposed endpoint normalization. The README correctly leaves the full caller theorem unimplemented."
    },
    {
      "check": "Hypothetical packet import and semantic consumer boundary",
      "result": "PASS_SOURCE_ONLY",
      "detail": "FrameContracts is an inert batch219 proposal import, absent as a current maintained library module. Its K215FrameEngine/FramedTemplates/KPathFrame closure still requires deliberate adoption and checks. Neither FrameCallers nor FrameRouteSound is needed by this prefix adapter. Current KSim has no RunContract, EdgeContract or SemanticCovered declarations; the pinned archived semantic consumer contains the proposed interfaces and must be narrowly rebased. The three-module classifier also remains uncompiled."
    },
